topics.description:
By default, a grid inside a grid item is **independent**: its tracks do not know about the outer grid. **Subgrid** lets the child use the parent's tracks, so nested content aligns across siblings.

### The classic problem
A row of cards, each with a title, text and button. Titles have different lengths, so the buttons sit at different heights. With subgrid, every card's internal rows share the same row lines, so titles, text and buttons align perfectly.

### Syntax
```css
.cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto;      /* implicit rows created by cards */
  gap: 1rem;
}
.card {
  display: grid;
  grid-row: span 3;                 /* card occupies three outer rows */
  grid-template-rows: subgrid;      /* inherits those three rows */
  gap: 0;
}
```

### Rules
- Use `subgrid` as the value of `grid-template-columns` and/or `grid-template-rows`.
- The subgrid item must **span** the tracks it wants to share.
- Gaps are inherited, but you can override `gap`.
- Line names from the parent are available inside.

### When to use
- Card grids with aligned internal parts.
- Forms where labels and inputs from different groups align.
- Complex page layouts where a child must participate in the page grid (full-bleed layouts).

### Support
Supported in all current major browsers (Firefox first, Chrome 117+, Safari 16+). Provide a graceful fallback (cards still work, only alignment is lost).

examples.css:
body { font-family: sans-serif; }
.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 10px; }
article { display: grid; grid-row: span 3; grid-template-rows: subgrid; gap: 6px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; background: #f8fafc; }
h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; }
p { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; }
button { align-self: end; border: 0; background: #2965f1; color: #fff; padding: 6px; border-radius: 6px; }

:root { --bg: #ffffff; --text: #0f172a; --card: #f1f5f9; --btn: #2965f1; color-scheme: light; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root:not([data-theme="light"]) { --bg: #0b1020; --text: #e2e8f0; --card: #1e293b; --btn: #60a5fa; color-scheme: dark; } }
:root[data-theme="dark"] { --bg: #0b1020; --text: #e2e8f0; --card: #1e293b; --btn: #60a5fa; color-scheme: dark; }
:root[data-theme="light"] { --bg: #ffffff; --text: #0f172a; --card: #f1f5f9; --btn: #2965f1; color-scheme: light; }
body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-family: sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 14px; transition: background .3s, color .3s; }
.card { background: var(--card); padding: 14px; border-radius: 10px; }
button { background: var(--btn); color: #fff; border: 0; padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 6px; }

examples.js:
const root = document.documentElement;
const isDark = () => root.dataset.theme
  ? root.dataset.theme === 'dark'
  : window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
document.getElementById('t').addEventListener('click', () => {
  root.dataset.theme = isDark() ? 'light' : 'dark';
});
